# build output
/build/
/build/logs/
obj/

# ★★ GROUND TRUTH IS LOCAL AND NEVER PUSHED (CLAUDE.md §2.2).
# docs/ground-truth/ holds the GIME reference and the AGI Specifications. They are
# third-party documents that live in the working tree and are not ours to redistribute.
# The .gitkeep is tracked (negated below) so the directory exists on a fresh clone and
# a citation like [ref: GIME-RM §10] has a home to point at.
#
# ★ CONSEQUENCE, and it is the reason this is a rule and not a convenience: a citation
# against a file in here is EXECUTOR-VERIFIABLE AND ORCHESTRATOR-UNVERIFIABLE. Absence
# from the public repo is NOT absence from the working tree (CLAUDE.md §2S.2).
docs/ground-truth/*
!docs/ground-truth/.gitkeep

# ★ GAME DATA IS THE USER'S AND IS NEVER COMMITTED (CLAUDE.md §2P).
# games/ holds MANIFESTS ONLY — checksums and version identification. VOL and DIR files
# are copyrighted, are the user's property, and are read-only to this project. A game
# file that reaches the index is a bug, not an oversight.
games/**
!games/manifests/
!games/manifests/.gitkeep
!games/manifests/*.md
!games/manifests/*.json
!games/manifests/*.tsv

# ★ THE ORACLE IS PINNED, NOT VENDORED (CLAUDE.md §2Q.1).
# oracle/ holds oracle/scummvm.pin, patches and dumps. A checked-in ScummVM tree starts
# feeling like source, and per CLAUDE.md §2 there is no source. Never vendor it.
oracle/scummvm/
oracle/src/
oracle/**/*.o
oracle/**/*.so
oracle/**/*.exe

# disk images and build artifacts — reproducible from tools/imgbuild/, never committed
*.dmk
*.dsk
*.jvc
*.vhd
*.bin
!content/*.bin

# python / logs / previews
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
harness/**/previews/
/build/previews/

# MAME writes cfg/ (coco3.cfg, default.cfg) into its CWD, which is the repo root when
# harness/smoke/run_*_test.sh runs. Emulator state, not project state.
/cfg/

# MAME writes snap/ (screenshots) into its CWD, same as cfg/.
/snap/

# MAME rewrites files in -cfg_directory on exit and drops a default.cfg there.
# The authored coco3.cfg templates are tracked; MAME's byproducts are not.
dist/mame-cfg/*/default.cfg

# git checkout-index --temp scratch (used by the .gitattributes CRLF round-trip check)
.merge_file_*


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ★★★ GAME-DATA HARDENING (P0.4) — COMMITTED BEFORE THE CoCo3 CORPUS ARRIVED, DELIBERATELY.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ★★★ THE ORDERING IS THE SAFETY PROPERTY, NOT THE PATTERN LIST.
# Game data pushed to a public repository CANNOT BE DELETED. A later `rm` takes it out of the
# working tree and leaves it in history, and the only real remedy is a history rewrite across
# three synchronised sibling repos (§2M) plus a force-push. So this block landed and was pushed
# BEFORE any archive was dropped into the repo root. Patterns added after the fact protect
# nothing that matters.
#
# This is defence in depth, not the primary control. The primary control is CLAUDE.md §2E's
# explicit-path staging — `git add -A` is forbidden, and this task is the one that earns that
# rule its keep. These patterns catch the case where someone forgets.
#
# ★ NOTE: .gitignore does NOT protect an already-tracked file, and does not stop `git add -f`.
# It stops the accident, not the intent.
#
# --- carrier formats: disk images and archives, AT ANY DEPTH (no leading slash) ------------
*.dsk
*.par
*.zip
*.os9
*.img
*.dmk
*.jvc
*.vhd
*.d77
*.hfe
# not named by the dispatch, added because an archive can arrive in any wrapper:
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.arc
*.lzh
#
# --- AGI resource files by NAME, at any depth ----------------------------------------------
# ★ These have no extension, so an extension rule cannot catch them. They are the actual game
# content: VOL files carry every LOGIC, PICTURE, VIEW and SOUND resource; the DIR files index
# them; words.tok is the parser vocabulary; object is the inventory table.
vol.*
*vol.[0-9]
*VOL.[0-9]
logdir
picdir
viewdir
snddir
words.tok
object
LOGDIR
PICDIR
VIEWDIR
SNDDIR
WORDS.TOK
OBJECT
# v3 combined-directory shapes (<prefix>dir, e.g. dmdir / vdir — P0.3 §4.2).
# ★ Deliberately broad: a v3 title names its directory file after its own prefix, so the set of
# possible names is open-ended and cannot be enumerated. The cost is that a future directory
# whose name ends in "dir" would also be ignored; the benefit is that no v3 title can slip
# through on a prefix nobody predicted. Safety wins here — and an intended file can always be
# added with `git add -f`, which is a visible act.
*dir
#
# --- Sierra's CoCo3 interpreter and OS-9 modules -------------------------------------------
# ★ Sierra's shipped interpreter is COPYRIGHTED CODE, not game data, and is likewise never
# committed. It is a comparison target only (dispatch §7 / backlog D-14).
CMDS/
MODULES/
OS9Boot
os9boot
#
# ★★ WHAT IS STILL ALLOWED THROUGH, and must stay allowed:
#   games/manifests/*.tsv  — checksums, sizes and version identification. NEVER content.
# That negation lives in the games/** block above and is not overridden here: no pattern in
# this section matches a .tsv, a .md or a .json.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
